# Stradivarius violin — buyable listings and acquisition channels

Compiled: 2026-05-12 (UTC). Source: public web search; this is **not** an exhaustive crawl of the entire internet. URLs and marketplace listings change or expire without notice. **“Antonius Stradivarius” labels on mass-market instruments are almost always German or factory copies, not Cremonese Stradivari.**

---

## 1. Authentic Antonio Stradivari violins (recent public sales — typically brokered or auctioned)

These were **offered for purchase** through named channels; many have **already sold**. Use the links for provenance, press, or to contact the same houses for future offerings.

| Instrument | Channel | Notes | URL |
|------------|---------|-------|-----|
| The Joachim–Ma, 1714 | Sotheby’s, New York | Auction 2025-02-07; estimate about USD 12–18M; widely reported sold about **USD 11.25M** (e.g. NPR). | https://www.sothebys.com/en/buy/auction/2025/the-joachim-ma-stradivarius-a-masterpiece-of-sound/antonio-stradivari-the-joachim-ma-violin |
| The McKay, c. 1737 | Kodner Galleries | Auction **2025-10-08**; reported sold about **USD 2.75M** including premium (trade press). | https://www.kodner.com/auctions/2025/10/08/stradivarius-violin-estate-jewelry-decoration/81 |
| da Vinci, ex Seidel, c. 1714 | Tarisio | Sold **2022-06-09**; reported about **USD 15.34M**. | https://tarisio.com/auctions/notable-sales/da-vinci-ex-seidel-stradivari-of-c-1714/ |
| Archive / provenance pages (not necessarily “for sale” now) | Tarisio Cozio | e.g. ‘Soil’ 1714, ‘Lord Dunraven’ 1710, ‘von Beckerath’ c. 1728 — reference entries. | https://tarisio.com/cozio-archive/ |

